; The pitch's fall across a sentence. Two cards a frame in: whether it starts a sentence (from sents) and its
; sentence's L (from spread); per frame out the pitch so far, 130 - q Hz, q = 30 f / L (f the frame in the
; sentence), at most 30. q moves by Bresenham: each frame adds 30 to qr and takes L away as often as it goes.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            frm     INP   ns       03-10: a frame; a new sentence starts q again
  04                    INP   l
  05                    CLA   ns
  06                    SUB   00
  07                    TAC   go
  08                    CLA   z
  09                    STO   q
  10                    STO   qr
  11            go      CLA   c130     11-35: 130 - q out, q on a frame
  12                    SUB   q
  13                    STO   b
  14                    OUT   b
  15                    CLA   q
  16                    SUB   c30
  17                    TAC   qu
  18                    JMP   frm
  19            qu      CLA   qr
  20                    ADD   c30
  21                    STO   qr
  22            ql      CLA   qr
  23                    SUB   l
  24                    TAC   qd
  25                    STO   qr
  26                    CLA   q
  27                    ADD   00
  28                    STO   q
  29                    JMP   ql
  30            qd      CLA   q
  31                    SUB   c30
  32                    TAC   frm
  33                    CLA   c30
  34                    STO   q
  35                    JMP   frm
  60            ns      DATA  0
  61            l       DATA  0
  62            q       DATA  0
  63            qr      DATA  0
  64            b       DATA  0
  65            z       DATA  0
  66            c130    DATA  130
  67            c30     DATA  30
